<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Celestino da Silva</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Celestino da Silva was a Portuguese army officer who governed Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timor">Timor</a> from 1894 to 1908. Through repeated military campaigns against the island's kingdoms he imposed colonial control over much of the interior, and he promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> plantations, partly through companies of his own. Resentment of the colonial order he built culminated in the Manufahi revolt of 1912.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-celestino-da-silva.jpg" alt="José Celestino da Silva" width="294" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jos%C3%A9_Celestino_da_Silva.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
